            <ArticleTitle>Giant intrasacral schwannoma forming a presacral mass: a report of an unusual cause of lumbosacral radiculopathy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>201-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Schwannomas are extremely rare tumours deriving from cells within the neurilemma. The authors report a case of giant intrasacral schwannoma presenting in the presacral region. The tumour presented with a lumbosacral pain and it was removed totally by two-stage surgical intervention. When seen five years after the second surgical intervention, the patient was asymptomatic. The rarity of such cases prompted this report.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
